/**
 * @defgroup StarVMCXGeometry xgeometry — Legacy AGE COMIS Geometry Assembler
 * @brief COMIS-based steering module for the STAR simulation geometry.
 *
 * `StarVMC/xgeometry/xgeometry.age` (4 645 lines) is the AGE source file that implements the
 * `geometry` steering module used by `starsim` when the AGML framework is active.  It is the
 * AGML 2 successor to `pams/geometry/geometry/geometry.g`.
 *
 * The file defines:
 * - A `CONSTRUCT` macro that dispatches to individual geometry modules at run-time using the
 *   COMIS functions `CsADDR` (address lookup) and `CsJCAL` (indirect call).
 * - A `replace [exe <NAME>;]` macro for every named detector configuration
 *   (e.g. `TPCE31`, `BTOFv8`, `EPDMv1`) and for every geometry tag
 *   (e.g. `y2023b`, `dev2022`), covering STAR running conditions from 2000 to 2025.
 * - The `geometry` AGE module (author: Pavel Nevski, August 1998) that parses the
 *   `DETP GEOM <tag>` command issued by `starsim`, executes the corresponding `exe` macro
 *   to set detector flags and configuration integers, and then invokes each active detector's
 *   constructor via `CsJCAL`.
 * - A thin `xgeometry` wrapper module that calls `geometry` and serves as the AgML entry point
 *   loaded into `xgeometry.so`.
 *
 * **Status:** Active for production tags y2016–y2025 and development tags (dev2022, ftsver*).
 * New detector subsystems should also define their configurations in
 * `StarVMC/Geometry/StarGeo.xml`; `xgeometry.age` is maintained for backward compatibility
 * with the legacy `DETP GEOM` steering interface.
 *
 * See `StarVMC/xgeometry/doc/README.md` for a complete description of the CONSTRUCT macro
 * mechanism, the REPLACE macro system, geometry tag definitions, and the relationship to
 * `pams/geometry/geometry/geometry.g`.
 */
